
Cruise Party: Track the Crowd
Problem Description
You are organizing a grand party on the luxury cruise ship "Cruise7". Guests are arriving and leaving throughout the evening.

You are given two arrays:

entry[] – where each element represents the number of people entering the party at a specific time.

exit[] – where each element represents the number of people leaving the party at that time (after the corresponding entry, not before).

Your job is to determine the maximum number of people present at the party at any given time.

Input:
Two integer arrays:

entry[] = {7, 0, 5, 1, 2}

exit[] = {1, 2, 1, 3, 4}

Each index represents a time unit (e.g. minute or hour). So at time i:

entry[i] people enter,

then exit[i] people leave.

Output: max=8
Print a single integer: the maximum number of people present at the party at any time.

7, 0, 5, 1, 2

1, 2, 1, 3, 4
==================
6  4  8  6  4
=====================================================================================================================================+



Problem Title: Jealous Children – Candy Comparison
Problem Statement:
A candy shop owner distributes chocolates to n children. Each child receives a certain number of chocolates.

Now, each child becomes jealous and wants to know how many chocolates others received in total, excluding their own.

Your task is to help the shopkeeper generate a new list, where each element represents the total number of chocolates given to all other children, excluding the current child.

Input Format:
First line: An integer n – the number of children

Second line: n space-separated integers – chocolates received by each child

Output Format:
Print n space-separated integers, where each value is:
total chocolates - chocolates of current child

Sample Test Cases:
Test Case 1:
Input:
4
5 6 4 7
Output:
17 16 18 15
Test Case 2:
3
1 2 3
Output:
5 4 3










































import java.util.*;
public class Cruize {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
		int n=sc.nextInt();
		int e[]=new int[n];
		int l[]=new int[n];
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
		{e[i]=sc.nextInt();
		}for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
		{
			l[i]=sc.nextInt();}
		int sum=0,max=0;
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++)//
		{
			sum+=e[i]-l[i];//7-1 //6-2 //9-1 //9-3//4
			max=Math.max(sum,max);//8,6=>8,6=>8,4=>8
		}
       System.out.println(max);
}}
